Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 05:07:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] dt-bindings: input: atmel,maxtouch: add atmel,enable-t97

The maXTouch-compatible touch controller on a Xiaomi Mi 4i (ferrari)
replacement panel does not report any touchscreen events until instance
0 of its T97 (PTC Key Set) object is enabled, and T97 is disabled again
after every reset or power cycle. The Xiaomi vendor driver enables T97
each time it wakes the controller.

This depends on the controller and the configuration it runs on a given
board, not on the maXTouch family: on other boards T97 is set up by the
stored configuration and must be left alone. The controller reports the
same family, variant and firmware version as a genuine mXT336T, so it
cannot be identified from its ID information, and its real part number
is not known, so there is no specific compatible to use.

Add a boolean property for boards whose controller needs T97 instance 0
to be enabled by the host.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 .../devicetree/bindings/input/atmel,maxtouch.yaml         | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/input/atmel,maxtouch.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/input/atmel,maxtouch.yaml
index 26ea78df27..186b644877 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/input/atmel,maxtouch.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/input/atmel,maxtouch.yaml
@@ -88,6 +88,14 @@ properties:
       - 2 # ATMEL_MXT_WAKEUP_GPIO
     default: 0
 
+  atmel,enable-t97:
+    type: boolean
+    description:
+      The controller does not report touchscreen events while instance 0 of
+      its T97 (PTC Key Set) object is disabled, and T97 is disabled after
+      every reset or power cycle, so T97 instance 0 has to be enabled each
+      time the controller is brought up or woken from deep sleep.
+
   wakeup-source: true
 
 required:
